n to  write some of these things please do it  okay maybe you don't have time but you  have money  you can be a sponsor  it is so easy to have so many excuses  why you don't want to try something new  or  get into a new field or get started  you can really talk people out of a lot  of excuses but you can't talk someone  out of not having enough money  so you could sponsor someone for a  course or a workshop like my brother did  for me  or some other creative way to use the  resource that you have  you can also send somebody to a  conference as we said before  a conference is so much more than just  talks and just  professional development you there's  networking you meet friends  there can be workshops you just get so  much more from a conference than  than you can really imagine it can be a  really great place  but as you know they can be really  expensive so if you  have some way to get an extra ticket or  if you're an organizer jsconf did a  really great job with these diversity  tickets where you could buy one and send  someone else with it  something like that is really awesome  and if you have a lot of time  you should become a mentor this is the  single most  important thing that you can do for  anyone who's starting out or changing  careers  it is just the biggest thing that you  can do to help someone  if you have somebody to trust and  somebody you can ask these questions to  and you can share your experiences with  and there's also so many different ways  that you can do this  it doesn't have to mean just one thing  so you could meet for lunch as often as  monthly or weekly whatever you can  commit to you could pair program with  people  you could simply offer advice by email  in my  in the last year or so i found out about  this program called  mentoring.is and it's a distributed  mentoring movement  and basically what it is is you add  slash mentoring to your personal website  and they give you a text and everything  that you can use to just  say to people hey i'm open to being a  mentor this is how to get in touch with  me  and it's a really great way if you don't  know how to get started or how to get  involved in your community you can  simply add this and start sharing it  and if you have space and time there's  more options  we need you to create safe spaces  what do i mean by that safe spaces can  be anything like a hackathon  a workshop a study group it could mean a  women-only group or some sort of  minority only group  and i want to make a point about this  there seems to be some controversy where  people think that these  whatever only spaces are exclusive but  they're not  they're actually inclusive what they do  is they include people who otherwise  would have been excluded whether they  would have felt uncomfortable or unsafe  or  just couldn't get in due to overcrowding  whatever reason it is it includes more  people who otherwise wouldn't have been  included and why are safe spaces  important  they're really important because this is  where you challenge yourself  and take risks and stretch your limits  you can't find out what new things you  can do if you don't feel comfortable  enough to try  new things so that's why safe spaces are  so important for us to have these  community spaces  and finally if you have courage i urge  you to tell your story  especially if you have a story that  doesn't fit the the mold of the  stereotypical kid who started  programming when he  could write and has been doing it his  entire life  i have a quote for you from a  documentary called misrepresentation  it says you cannot be what you cannot  see  so of course there are exceptions but if  you  can be a role model or a hero for  somebody where they can identify with  something with you  and if you're a little bit different  than than other people  that can be a really amazing amazing  way to help out by just becoming a  figure for people  so what now  i'd like to take one moment to give a  shout out to hard work and to  acknowledge the hard work that i did put  in and that other people like me have  put in because even with all the help in  the world it wouldn't have been possible  and i just think it's important to to  acknowledge  and i also have one more quote for you  it's by tal ben shahar who's a  positive psychologist from harvard and  he says  there's so much benefit to the person  who contributes to others that i often  think there is no more selfish act than  a generous act  so that means that anything you do for  other people  you're really doing for yourself and any  of these ways that you can help out you  will feel a reward  and it will feel good and i'm i can  promise you that  so now i would like you to please return  to your villages  and make some programmers  thank you  thank you i have some resources for you  i will tweet it out later it's just got  some different things like what i use to  learn some programming the mentoring  link  different diversity groups if you're  interested in learning more about how to  diversify in your own company  and some different coding group for kids  and so again i would like to say thank  you to everybody who's helped me  thank you for listening and thank you  from the future for all of the people  that you will help  thank you for the people you've been  helping and thank you for everyone  you've helped already  thanks
 

